  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A CT head scan is performed to evaluate the brain mass and any new changes. The findings show unchanged mass effect and edema around the large right parietal mass."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-321b66316d11f34afdca9611a9f48664</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MRI HEAD SCAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An MRI head scan is conducted to further evaluate the extent of the ring-enhancing brain mass with edema. The findings reveal a large right parietal mass with complex appearance, substantial edema, and midline shift."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-321b66316d11f34afdca9611a9f48664</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIZZINESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SYMPTOM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dizziness is a symptom experienced by the patient, along with headache and visual disturbances."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-321b66316d11f34afdca9611a9f48664</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SILVERY SPECTORS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SYMPTOM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The patient reports seeing 'silvery spectors' in her vision, which could indicate visual disturbances."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-321b66316d11f34afdca9611a9f48664</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GBM METASTASIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONDITION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"GBM metastasis refers to the spread of glioblastoma multiforme to other parts of the body, indicated by the presence of ring-enhancing brain mass with edema."&gt;</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-321b66316d11f34afdca9611a9f48664</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RIGHT PARIETAL LESION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Right Parietal Lesion is a mass located in the right parietal lobe of the brain, which may represent either a primary or metastatic brain neoplasm."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f8dc58072829c395689fe28e9508edb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEFT TEMPORAL LESION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Left Temporal Lesion is a mass located in the left temporal lobe of the brain, which could have alternative diagnoses including hemorrhage or a calcified meningioma."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f8dc58072829c395689fe28e9508edb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LEFT OCCIPITAL LESION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Left Occipital Lesion is a mass located in the left occipital lobe of the brain, which could have alternative diagnoses including an inflammatory or ischemic process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2f8dc58072829c395689fe28e9508edb</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DR. &quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Dr. is a medical professional involved in the diagnosis and treatment of the patient's brain lesions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dr. is a medical professional who referred the patient to the inpatient unit for stabilization and evaluation for ECT."</data>
